{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"280f02e2-44a8-4362-b34a-fb3934800143","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented a proper caching split for the system prompt.\n\n- **What changed:** `build_system` in `bot.py` now returns **two** system messages:\n  1. The immutable `INSTRUCTIONS` with `cache_control.type = \"static\"` (never evicted).\n  2. The per‑athlete context (`athlete_context(a, today)`) with `cache_control.type = \"ephemeral\"`.\n\n- **Why it fixes the issue:** Previously the whole prompt (including static instructions) was cached as *ephemeral*, so any `save_fact` write caused the static instructions to be re‑cached and charged again. By separating static instructions into a static cache entry, only the dynamic athlete‑specific part is refreshed, eliminating the extra token cost after memory writes.\n\nFor a full description of the changes, see the generated artifact:\n\n[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/280f02e2-44a8-4362-b34a-fb3934800143/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":48.64555,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":17979,"output_tokens":3162,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":127424,"total_tokens":21141}}}
